1	//! gpu_ecm.rs — Lenstra elliptic-curve factorization on the GPU, any width.
2	//!
3	//! One Montgomery curve per thread over a Montgomery field whose limb count is
4	//! chosen to fit N, so there is no size ceiling on the input. Each thread scales
5	//! its point by the product of prime powers up to B1 with the x-only ladder,
6	//! then takes gcd(Z, N); a curve whose order mod a factor p is B1-smooth drives
7	//! Z to 0 mod p and the gcd reveals p. Thousands of curves at once, first factor
8	//! wins. The arithmetic is verified against BigUint at each width before use.
